{"id": "EUVD-2026-102943", "enisaUuid": "c97a064d-ad97-3a97-9cf4-3b2c9e2d986c", "description": "MariaDB server is a community developed fork of MySQL server. From 10.6.1 until 10.6.28, 10.11.19, 11.4.13, 11.8.9, 12.3.3, and 13.0.2, SHOW CREATE SERVER, SHOW CREATE USER, and mariadb-dump are affected because each does not consistently quote identifiers and values when serializing SQL. A low-privileged attacker can trigger the issue when an attacker-created object with crafted identifiers or values is included in SHOW output or a dump, then create an object with crafted identifiers or values so generated SQL contains injected statements and execute attacker-injected SQL when the poisoned output is applied. This issue is fixed in versions 10.6.28, 10.11.19, 11.4.13, 11.8.9, 12.3.3, and 13.0.2.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T16:37:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T12:42:14", "baseScore": 7.7, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:L/UI:R/S:C/C:N/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://github.com/MariaDB/server/security/advisories/GHSA-wxr3-wm3p-7w6p", "https://github.com/MariaDB/server/commit/2b28d1c424104429eeed43115ee6d8a803671d52", "https://github.com/MariaDB/server/commit/3646569225758c8225e7342783d775ef7c7570e5", "https://github.com/MariaDB/server/commit/5acb43522863c9bd6b91f354104ea247bf513e9a", "https://github.com/MariaDB/server/commit/9d4ffe23b25808f7858b2dc48106fbd60cf0e513", "https://github.com/MariaDB/server/commit/d5d741a3076f911b468518d6b06a917593498c5b", "https://github.com/MariaDB/server/releases/tag/mariadb-10.11.19", "https://github.com/MariaDB/server/releases/tag/mariadb-10.6.28", "https://github.com/MariaDB/server/releases/tag/mariadb-11.4.13", "https://github.com/MariaDB/server/releases/tag/mariadb-11.8.9", "https://github.com/MariaDB/server/releases/tag/mariadb-12.3.3", "https://github.com/MariaDB/server/releases/tag/mariadb-13.0.2", "https://jira.mariadb.org/browse/MDEV-39776", "https://jira.mariadb.org/browse/MDEV-39818", "htt